{
  "format": "waddle.behavior/v0",
  "name": "dual_write_detection",
  "description": "Pins N14 and the FSM.md §3 advisory-enforcement note: during bypass on an ADVISORY-lease integration (reached claimed-while-stalled style: HOLD_FIRST engage, caller stall past the 500000000 ns threshold, teleop pumped via the declared send verb), sustained divergence between the commanded trajectory (near-zero station-keeping teleop deltas) and proprioception (four samples over ~200 ms with growing joint drift — someone else is writing) must freeze via hold and alert: a DualWriteDetected event with action_taken VERB_HOLD and a persisted divergence trace_ref, plus the request_verb{VERB_HOLD} effect. The episode must NOT terminate — it stays INTERVENTION with the gate still in BYPASS (the hold is an output condition, not a mode change). Judgment calls: as in handoff_hold_first, an `effect` emission is asserted on the gate target (the composed FSM's effects remain observable); the detection window and divergence threshold are implementation-declared, so the fixture provides drift (0 to 0.5 rad on the left arm's first joint at rising velocity) far beyond any plausible bound and allows 100 ms for detection after the final sample; part names 'left'/'right' assumed from the bimanual fixture.",
